Written from origin develop `f6669623ccae5ab445be6e0e73fb4f19ae2c89d1` (measured by `git ls-remote origin develop` at 10:14 AEST 2026-09-18 — this is #1032's merge commit and it IS the tip).
`Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/src/services/redis.ts` read WHOLE at that tip: blob `47659ee9c9f06acf9ac64e09b2dc207113ba92ea`, **732 lines** (`wc -l`; the input builder prints 733, counting the trailing newline).

## THE MODE — read this twice

**CODE_PATCH.** This service runs **VITEST** (`vi`, not `jest`). Your diff contains EXACTLY TWO files:
1. `services/api-gateway/src/services/redis.ts` — ONE hunk (one `-` line, three `+` lines).
2. `services/api-gateway/src/__tests__/ks1233-in-redis-mode-platform-settings-expires.test.ts` — ONE NEW file.
**Nothing else.** Not `routes/admin.ts`, not `routes/verification.ts`, not any existing test. Two files, no more, no fewer.
Write the paths as `services/api-gateway/...` — NEVER `Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/...`.

## What is wrong (one paragraph)

In Redis mode the gateway stores **platform-settings** — the object that carries every connector's `allowedDocumentTypes` allow-list — with a **24 hour TTL and nothing that refreshes it**. `redis.ts:22-29` defines `TTL.privacy: 86400`; `redis.ts:680-687` `setNotificationSettings` writes `notif:<key>` with `setex(fullKey, TTL.privacy, …)`; and the ONLY writer of `platform-settings` is `routes/admin.ts:1127` (`PUT /api/admin/settings`). So 24 hours after the last admin settings write the key is gone, `getNotificationSettings('platform-settings')` returns null, `routes/verification.ts:1214-1216` turns that into `integrations []` — **no restriction** — and every restricted connector silently becomes unrestricted. It is the same fail-open class as the container fail-open filed beside it, and local runs never show it because the no-Redis fallback is a `Map` with no TTL at all. **The decision this brief takes (Wednesday, on the ticket's "the owner decides"): platform-settings is CONFIGURATION, not a cache entry, so it is written WITHOUT an expiry. Every other `notif:` key keeps the 24 h TTL it has today** — the change is as narrow as it can be, in the same spirit as the KS-791 exception in `contentType.ts`.

NOT in this task: the read side (`verification.ts` turning a missing settings object into "no restriction"), the `TTL.privacy` constant itself (four other call sites at `:350`, `:383`, `:409`, `:434` depend on it and are correct), and anything touching auth, MFA or OAuth.

## Where (line-keyed — every **must change** line must appear as a `-` line AT ITS NUMBER)

- `:682` — (correct) `if (isRedisAvailable()) {` — the Redis-mode branch of `setNotificationSettings`. Stays, as your leading context line.
- `:683` — **must change** `await redisClient!.setex(fullKey, TTL.privacy, JSON.stringify(data));` — the 24 h write. This is the ONE line you remove. NOTE: this exact text also occurs at `:350` in a different function; yours is the one at **683**, and the trailing context below pins it.
- `:684` — (correct) `} else {` — the in-memory fallback. Stays, as trailing context.
- `:685` — (correct) `notificationSettingsStore.set(key, data);` — the fallback write; unchanged and untouched by this ticket. Stays, as trailing context. This line occurs exactly ONCE in the file and is what makes your hunk land at 683 and not at 350.

